WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.966
Where did you start from?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.170
From Dawu... Dawu. Oh man.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.440
You just headed out?
No, not really.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:47.647
I stayed in Jinlun yesterday.
I camped out there with my tent.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:53.520
Honestly, I shouldn't have brought the mirrorless camera.
It's just too heavy.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.989
And I barely even used the tripod.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.737
A real-world look at the Insta360 Ace Pro 2

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:15.608
after using it for three months. With the Ace Pro 2,

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:19.746
its powerful hardware and software make travel filming

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:23.216
way easier and a lot more fun, without having to rely on

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.519
heavy, expensive mirrorless camera gear.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:30.900
So, can the Ace Pro 2 really replace a mirrorless camera?

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.359
In some ways, yes. Let's check it out.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:47.173
I accidentally dropped my Sony ZV-E10 II camera.

00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.519
Action cameras keep getting better, and image quality

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.689
is now a pretty solid option. Night shooting is stronger too.

00:02:35.689 --> 00:02:38.558
Action cameras are way more drop-resistant than mirrorless cameras.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:42.529
That's one big reason I'm leaning toward action cameras.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.897
I chose the Ace Pro 2.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.167
Why did I choose the Ace Pro 2?

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.502
Because it has really strong night-shooting performance.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.973
Back when I used a GoPro, once nighttime came,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.608
I had to put it away. Because GoPro

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.411
night footage was rough—tons of noise,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.546
and the image was really dark.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.716
The Ace Pro 2 fits my needs perfectly.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.586
And in this second generation, it integrates a lot of things,

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.689
like this wind guard and the high-capacity battery.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.227
It also has a flip screen, which is super handy for framing.

00:03:14.361 --> 00:03:16.563
It kind of gives you that mirrorless-camera feel.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.399
A lot of mirrorless cameras have flip screens like this.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:24.371
For me, this is basically

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:27.173
a filming tool and a framing lifesaver.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.844
First, let's look at the Ace Pro 2's main selling points.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:42.880
When it comes to action camera selling points,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:46.493
they usually print them right on the box.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.928
Let's take a look.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.531
Ace Pro 2. This one is made in collaboration with Leica,

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:57.437
the German camera brand. It has a Leica lens.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:00.240
An 8K action camera with an AI chip.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:04.440
That's the message they're showing on the front.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.546
Video, a flip-screen shot out in the wild,

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.848
and an off-road vehicle going off-road.

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:13.119
This is the dual-battery version, with two batteries in the box.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.589
So the front highlights Leica, 8K, and the AI chip.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:20.727
Now let's look at the side.

00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:25.432
Here it talks about wind noise reduction.

00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:28.435
For wind noise reduction, they designed this part

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.671
with a metal mesh and a small sponge inside.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.673
It's built right in,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.109
so we don't need to bring a furry wind muff anymore.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.212
With older GoPros, you had to add an outer frame

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.147
and a furry wind muff. This one doesn't need that.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:44.840
The integration is really good and super convenient.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.586
You won't get that annoying wind noise.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:58.131
Bike camping northbound against the northeast monsoon.

00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:04.838
Can you hear the difference in audio quality?

00:05:08.742 --> 00:05:12.712
The second feature is the flip screen.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.515
When you're filming a dog, the flip screen

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.917
lets you adjust to a better angle.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.586
You don't have to squat down, so it's much easier.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:20.920
This is really convenient.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:24.758
Second, for vlogging—selfies where you talk to yourself.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.280
For selfies, of course you want your face in the shot.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:31.464
With the flip screen, your framing is much more accurate.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.233
And the screen is pretty big too.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:38.980
The third feature is stabilization.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:42.235
With it on or off, the difference is huge.

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:45.705
Insta360's stabilization tech is already really good.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:52.912
Not only daytime stabilization—night stabilization works too.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:57.584
They don't hold back the latest tech; they give it to users.

00:06:57.584 --> 00:07:02.589
No wonder more and more people love Insta360.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.526
The fourth feature is waterproofing.

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:09.229
It goes down to 12 meters.

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:12.999
That's something an outdoor camera should definitely have.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:17.700
In real use, if we're outdoors and it rains,

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:21.541
this waterproofing really comes in handy.

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.977
We probably won't actually dive 12 meters with it,

00:07:23.977 --> 00:07:26.513
but basic rain protection has to be solid.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:43.897
Ace Pro 2 sitting outside directly in the rain.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.621
The fifth feature is AI auto-editing software.

00:08:08.822 --> 00:08:11.424
It's great for lazy editing and quickly making Shorts.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:14.894
It finds the highlight moments from your trip

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:16.363
and edits them together automatically.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:21.167
So these are the five key points on the side: wind noise reduction,

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.970
flip screen, stabilization, 12-meter waterproofing,

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.139
and AI editing. Five big selling points.

00:08:30.377 --> 00:08:34.147
Over here are more technical specs.

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.483
First is the larger image sensor.

00:08:36.783 --> 00:08:39.252
A larger sensor means better results on cloudy days or at night.

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:42.355
I'm pretty happy with that.

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:45.910
Besides the larger sensor,

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.260
it also has dual AI chips.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.497
That gives you excellent image quality.

00:08:50.964 --> 00:08:54.401
It probably dynamically adjusts things like saturation

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:55.702
and brightness in your video.

00:08:57.337 --> 00:09:00.740
Next, even in low light,

00:09:01.174 --> 00:09:03.777
the Ace Pro 2 still performs really well.

00:09:03.777 --> 00:09:06.212
This is the Ace Pro 2. This one is another brand—

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.800
Brand D, maybe?

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.350
By another brand, I mean Brand D. We'll leave that aside for now.

00:09:13.186 --> 00:09:23.930
Drastic lighting changes between indoors and outdoors.

00:09:34.874 --> 00:09:43.750
No streetlights, total darkness. Good thing I had the AP2.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:48.955
A night-shooting beast ❤️

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:53.960
At dusk.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:59.320
Stabilization, light, and audio—sugoi.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:05.380
Streetlights crossing through the night.

00:10:12.312 --> 00:10:19.786
Kenting land crab ecological corridor, with lighting control.

00:10:20.787 --> 00:10:25.792
The lighting on site was uneven and still very dark.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:32.265
It also works for filming the Xuhai sunrise in low light.

00:10:32.265 --> 00:10:34.801
Use the flip screen to frame the sun.

00:10:38.705 --> 00:10:43.710
At 5:30 a.m. in low light, Xuhai's beauty comes back to life!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:51.510
AP2 and X5, both with dual AI chips—best buddies.

00:10:58.925 --> 00:11:03.930
A highlight moment from my biking life.

00:11:04.197 --> 00:11:09.202
If low-light footage doesn't fall apart, it's worth the money.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:21.470
Night mode gives night owls like you plenty to love.

00:11:21.648 --> 00:11:26.653
With a good camera, don't overthink the tech. Just buy it.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.893
The fourth one is Active HDR.

00:11:33.893 --> 00:11:35.695
Active HDR means that

00:11:35.962 --> 00:11:38.531
when you're outdoors and the brightness gets high,

00:11:38.531 --> 00:11:41.735
it automatically corrects it so your video doesn't get overexposed.

00:11:59.986 --> 00:12:04.991
S-HDR solves the problem of video being afraid of both dark and bright scenes.

00:12:11.631 --> 00:12:16.636
Oh no—the lawn mower.

00:12:16.703 --> 00:12:18.905
The fifth one is the wide field of view.

00:12:19.272 --> 00:12:23.643
Its field of view reaches 157 degrees.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.745
That means you can see a lot wider.

00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:30.830
Especially when cycling or outdoors, seeing wider

00:12:30.383 --> 00:12:32.752
just makes you feel better.

00:12:33.186 --> 00:12:36.556
You won't feel trapped inside a tiny frame,

00:12:36.556 --> 00:12:39.125
unable to show the scene you're actually in.

00:12:40.427 --> 00:12:44.330
😀 Mic Pro

00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:53.606
Let's look at the 157-degree big scene.

00:13:03.216 --> 00:13:08.655
They also did a collaboration with MotoGP rider Marc Márquez,

00:13:08.655 --> 00:13:11.791
a special racing edition.

00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:15.228
That version features Márquez's racing number,

00:13:15.495 --> 00:13:17.297
MM93.

00:13:17.297 --> 00:13:18.732
Mine is the standard version.

00:13:18.732 --> 00:13:23.737
The silly opening animation in this video pays tribute to Márquez.

00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:32.746
A MotoGP legend: first title at 20,
eight-time champion, and holder of 30+ records.

00:13:33.947 --> 00:13:38.151
You can see the design. This is the big eye,

00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:42.756
and inside it says Leica—Leica camera, Leica lens.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:50.830
Let's power it on and check the startup speed.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:52.232
The speed is pretty fast too.

00:13:52.232 --> 00:13:53.800
Sometimes we want to capture something,

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.337
like birds, dogs, small animals, or kids

00:13:57.337 --> 00:13:59.439
suddenly running into the frame, so startup needs to be fast.

00:14:00.273 --> 00:14:03.209
This front display area

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:04.744
has a bright indicator light.

00:14:05.945 --> 00:14:09.649
This is the metal mesh for wind noise reduction.

00:14:10.116 --> 00:14:11.785
You can slide it open and replace it.

00:14:12.752 --> 00:14:16.990
This is the Insta360 logo.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:24.264
The logo is right here. Let's keep looking. The mesh—

00:14:24.264 --> 00:14:27.000
and this is the power button. It's very simple.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.735
There are only two buttons. This is one of them.

00:14:29.269 --> 00:14:31.237
Open this side and you get the memory card slot.

00:14:31.638 --> 00:14:34.374
The memory card slot and the USB-C charging port.

00:14:35.542 --> 00:14:37.877
Same thing: close it properly before diving.

00:14:38.678 --> 00:14:43.616
Let's keep looking. This is the battery.

00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:50.256
The battery is here. Okay, let's check the back.

00:14:50.256 --> 00:14:55.295
This is the screen, and it flips up.

00:14:55.295 --> 00:14:58.431
The screen is also pretty large.

00:14:59.299 --> 00:15:06.390
Touch control feels really smooth, and it has tons of features.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:08.341
You can use gestures and voice control.

00:15:08.341 --> 00:15:10.610
It also has a lot of Bluetooth connectivity options.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.947
And if you use their products, you can basically build

00:15:13.947 --> 00:15:15.615
your own little ecosystem.

00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:25.910
Video, night video, video, free-frame video, motion timelapse, timelapse,

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:29.662
dashcam mode, loop recording, slow motion, star-lapse,

00:15:29.662 --> 00:15:36.236
burst interval, photo, photo-video, night video.

00:15:36.236 --> 00:15:37.470
It gives you a lot of functions.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:41.508
Night video and video—normally, I use standard

00:15:41.508 --> 00:15:42.976
video

00:15:42.976 --> 00:15:47.213
and night video. Those are the two modes I use the most.

00:15:47.213 --> 00:15:47.714
I use them all the time.

00:15:48.548 --> 00:15:49.983
It also has lossless zoom.

00:15:53.486 --> 00:15:56.456
Let's look at the Ace Pro 2's flip screen.

00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:58.792
There are latches on both sides of the flip screen.

00:15:59.893 --> 00:16:01.761
Press the latches down and open it.

00:16:02.595 --> 00:16:06.320
It has some damping,

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:10.937
and the benefit is, when I'm shooting from this low angle,

00:16:10.937 --> 00:16:13.573
I can lift the screen up

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:16.910
and see the shot I want to capture.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:19.446
I don't have to squat down.

00:16:19.813 --> 00:16:22.515
Now we're going to film Danbo, but I don't know

00:16:22.882 --> 00:16:27.454
if the shot is good or if Danbo is centered.

00:16:27.454 --> 00:16:29.723
At times like this, the flip screen helps us see

00:16:29.723 --> 00:16:33.326
whether the framing is lined up. Okay, let's shoot.

00:16:33.393 --> 00:16:38.231
Start recording. See, Danbo is right here.

00:16:38.231 --> 00:16:42.135
Then it just walks, walks, walks, walks.

00:16:42.202 --> 00:16:47.240
See? Our framing becomes much more accurate.

00:16:51.711 --> 00:16:54.447
Let's look at the Insta360

00:16:54.447 --> 00:16:55.615
Ace Pro 2 connector.

00:16:58.585 --> 00:17:06.590
Attach it like this. See? It's that convenient.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.270
Super convenient.

00:17:08.294 --> 00:17:10.630
If you buy their whole ecosystem,

00:17:11.398 --> 00:17:12.399
this is the kind of benefit you get.

00:17:13.633 --> 00:17:15.935
I also really like using the X5.

00:17:18.104 --> 00:17:22.776
The X5 is great whether you're riding a motorcycle or a bicycle.

00:17:23.643 --> 00:17:25.780
Using 360 footage is safer,

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:27.781
and you can still capture everything. That's the X5.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:33.620
So, is their Ace Pro 2 convenient or not?

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:45.598
Insta360 has also released a 360 panoramic drone.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:55.750
And recently, they also released a wireless Bluetooth microphone.

00:17:57.811 --> 00:18:03.750
So choosing which ecosystem to go with becomes pretty important.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.719
Now is a good time to join Insta360.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.722
They have 360 cameras,

00:18:08.855 --> 00:18:10.457
action cameras, the king of night shooting,

00:18:11.424 --> 00:18:13.493
the Antigravity A1 panoramic drone,

00:18:13.493 --> 00:18:20.734
and wireless Bluetooth microphones too.

00:18:22.635 --> 00:18:25.271
Join the Insta360 family.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:34.314
Let's look at the Ace Pro 2 charging system.

00:18:34.914 --> 00:18:36.883
The battery opens from here.

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:40.720
It also has this thoughtful design that shows when it's not closed properly.

00:18:40.987 --> 00:18:42.222
If you see orange, it means it isn't closed right.

00:18:43.323 --> 00:18:49.129
The battery is 1800 mAh.

00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:51.731
An 1800 mAh battery.

00:18:51.731 --> 00:18:55.402
This is the charging case. I'll put it in to charge.

00:18:57.971 --> 00:19:00.540
If you use PD fast charging,

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.475
it can charge to 80% in 20 minutes.

00:19:02.842 --> 00:19:05.278
So if you run out of power, just take a quick roadside break,

00:19:05.712 --> 00:19:08.515
and pretty soon you'll have 80% battery to use.

00:19:12.285 --> 00:19:15.210
Alright, that's my three-month review

00:19:15.555 --> 00:19:18.240
of the Insta360 Ace Pro 2.

